  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the scene through the hateful framing of the meme",
  "description": "The user is not explicitly projected onto a specific visual, textual, or scene element via deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me'. However, the meme's overall intent and structure create an implicit projection: the viewer is positioned as the recipient of the hateful message, being manipulated into seeing the juxtaposed portraits and text as a coherent, damning narrative about Obama and Islam. The user is thus projected onto the entire scene ('juxtaposed_portraits') as the intended audience for the false equivalence and fear-mongering. The user is implicitly 'you' — the one being shown the 'truth' (according to the meme) that Obama is 'islam's trojan horse' — making the user a passive recipient of the projection.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
